@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# Nix TEE Attestation
+
+Hardware-attested builds for Nix: every derivation output carries a
+binding record v1 certificate, and builds refuse to start unless every
+direct input is attested (or bootstrapped).
+
+## Binding record v1
+
+```json
+{
+  "version": 1,
+  "drv": "/nix/store/....drv",
+  "outputs": { "out": "sha256-..." },
+  "inputs": ["sha256-...", "sha256-..."],
+  "binding": "sha256-...",
+  "attestation": { "type": "tdx", "quote": "<base64>" }
+}
+```
+
+Certificates are stored as `<output-nar-hash-sri>.json` in
+`attestation-store`.
+
+## Nix configuration
+
+```ini
+require-attestation = true
+substitute = false
+attestation-store = /var/lib/nix-attestations
+attestation-verifier = /usr/local/bin/nix-attestation-verify
+post-build-hook = /usr/local/bin/nix-certifier
+attestation-bootstrap-inputs = sha256-... sha256-...
+```
+
+## Bootstrap inputs
+
+The first compiler cannot be attested. Pin and pre-seed:
+
+```bash
+nix-store --add-fixed sha256 bootstrap-tools.tar.xz
+chmod +x busybox && nix-store --add-fixed --recursive sha256 busybox
+```
+
+Add their NAR hashes to `attestation-bootstrap-inputs`.
+
+## Development (stub mode)
+
+Without TDX hardware:
+
+```bash
+export ATTESTATION_STUB_MODE=1
+```
+
+## Binary cache sidecars
+
+Substituters fetch `{hashPart}.attestation.json` and `{hashPart}.attestation.sig`
+(same 32-character hash as `{hashPart}.narinfo`).
+
+`nix-copy-closure` over `ssh://` (serve protocol 2.9) sends those two files
+**before** the NAR. Missing local sidecars or a remote serve older than 2.9
+is an error (`attestation-require-sidecar-on-copy`, default true); the NAR
+is not sent. The remote `nix-store --serve --write` verifies the
+Ed25519 cache signature (`trusted-public-keys`, fingerprint
+`attestation:1;<store-path>;<narHash-SRI>;<sha256 of JSON>`) and the
+binding record. Only then is the sidecar written and the NAR imported.
+With `require-attestation = true` on the receiver, a NAR without a
+prior verified sidecar is rejected (except bootstrap hashes).
+
+Receive-side `nix.conf` (Harmonia host), later HTTP ingest can reuse the same
+keys:
+
+```ini
+require-attestation = true
+attestation-require-cache-signature = true
+attestation-harmonia-dir = /var/lib/harmonia-attest
+trusted-public-keys = harmonia-1:BASE64...
+attestation-bootstrap-inputs = sha256-...
+```
+
+Both machines need this fork’s `nix-store`. Stock Nix advertises serve 2.8
+and the sidecar is skipped.
+
+Patched Harmonia (`C:\nixDocs\freshNix\harmonia`, or the WSL clone) serves
+`/{hash}.attestation.json` and `/{hash}.attestation.sig` from
+`attestation_dir` (default `/var/lib/harmonia-attest`) on the **same**
+substituter URL as `.narinfo` / NAR. No nginx path split.
+
+If NARs live under `outputs/nars/` (not yet in the local Nix store),
+register **every** path in that export (`index.json` `packages`, any
+root — not hardcoded to one package), then copy that export's `root`
+closure:
+
+```bash
+python3 contrib/attestation/ingest-nars-to-store.py \
+  --outputs ~/dev_test_docker/test_temp/tmp/outputs \
+  --nix-store ~/nixfresh/nix/outputs/out/bin/nix-store \
+  --copy-to ssh://harmoniatest@<22.04-IP>
+```
+
+`nix-store --import-nar` writes `{hashPart}.attestation.json` + `.sig` next
+to the valid path. `nix-copy-closure` over `ssh://` (serve 2.9) sends those
+files before each NAR. The Harmonia host must run this fork's
+`nix-store --serve --write` (stock 2.8 skips sidecars). Harmonia then
+serves both from the store + `attestation-harmonia-dir`.
+
+## Docker
+
+See `docker/` for the two-layer image build (`nix-tee-base` + package builder).
